<figure class="pipeline-map">
 <figcaption><span>System architecture</span><h3>Three image-derived inputs meet the mechanics model</h3></figcaption>
 <div class="input">RGB frame <small>Original image coordinates</small></div>
 <div class="branches">
  <section><b>01 · Crack geometry</b><h4>Crack segmentation</h4><p>Mask → skeleton → branches → assembled paths</p><strong>Trace length · orientation</strong><small>Visible and inferred portions recorded separately</small></section>
  <section><b>02 · Member geometry</b><h4>MobileSAM</h4><p>Offset prompts → surface mask → boundary chord</p><strong>Member extent W<sub>px</sub></strong><small>Prompts come from branch 01. Requires the relevant physical boundaries.</small></section>
  <section><b>03 · Physical scale</b><h4>Depth / calibration</h4><p>Metric depth + intrinsics, or a known reference</p><strong>Scale s in mm/px</strong><small>Aligned depth; suitable view geometry</small></section>
 </div>
 <div class="handoff"><b>Interpretation & calibration</b><p>Convert lengths to mm; inspect topology, edge connectivity and boundary visibility.</p><small>This is a modelling requirement. The prototype's heuristics do not guarantee it.</small></div>
 <div class="mechanics-inputs"><div><b>External inputs</b><p>Applied stress σ<br/>Material properties · toughness</p></div><div><b>Offline PINN solves</b><p>Selected a/W configurations<br/>Stored geometry factors F(a/W)</p></div></div>
 <div class="output"><b>Per-crack mechanics evaluation</b><p>Geometry + load + geometry factor → K<sub>I</sub> and K<sub>I</sub>/K<sub>IC</sub></p><small>Analytical fallback is reported separately. This post covers the perception side.</small></div>
</figure>
